#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#This run is from the CPAR archive CarSim_Kinematical_Preview.cpar.
#
#This example shows ABS braking behavior on a split-mu surface. This particular run is made to compare different options for numerical integration and linking with Simulink. Outputs are written every time step. The run is stopped after 1.5s because the behavior of interest can be seen the the plot of actuator pressure for one wheel.
#
#This specific run uses the built-in ABS controller and a very small time step (16 kHz frequency). The very small time step is used to establish a "true" baseline.
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

